  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q79-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Factorise $x^4+3x^3+6x^2+6x+4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x^2+x+2)(x^2+2x+2)$.\n\nComplete $(x^2+2)^2$, then group and factor.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4+3x^3+6x^2+6x+4&=(x^4+4x^2+4)+(3x^3+6x)+2x^2\\\\x^4+3x^3+6x^2+6x+4&=(x^2+2)^2+3x(x^2+2)+2x^2.\\end{align*}$$\nLet $u=x^2+2$. Since $1+2=3$ and $1\\cdot2=2$,\n$$u^2+3xu+2x^2=(u+x)(u+2x).$$\nSubstituting back gives\n$$x^4+3x^3+6x^2+6x+4=(x^2+x+2)(x^2+2x+2).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
